nodecode-commandcode is a rewrite of NanamiMio's NanamiMio/hermes-commandcode-oauth:
https://github.com/NanamiMio/hermes-commandcode-oauth
commit e51eb61613604aefbcf3203c8fcce531706232ee
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 NanamiMio (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the provider itself, as one Nodecode cell. transport.py became
wire.lisp -- the /alpha/generate request body (the workspace config block, the
turn's messages as typed parts, one system string, tools as input_schema
declarations), the CLI's client headers, the NDJSON event reader with the
in-stream error and the fail-closed end of a stream, and the usage split into
prompt, cached prompt and output. auth.py's CLI credential read became
PROVIDER.LISP's CLI-KEY (read only, the CLI's own file is never written) and
__init__.py's credential ladder became the :CREDENTIAL hook. model_metadata.py
became models.json, and the catalog row and the account's model listing
(/provider/v1/models?view=client) became the catalog and listing hooks.

Left out: the Hermes-only halves of the original, because Nodecode has its own
for each. The browser loopback sign-in to the studio (a 5959 listener, the
state check, the credential pool) is replaced by the core's /connect and by
importing the CLI's key; credential pooling, refresh, plan-lock filtering of
the catalog, the account-usage snapshot for a usage view, the failover
classifier and the fallback_models property bridge have no Nodecode seam to
port to, and the core's own model catalog, retry policy and picker stand in
for them. The plugin's smoke script and its test suite are not carried over.
